Managing your Providers

# Manage Providers

Providers you can add:

  * Docker (docker)
  * Podman (podman)
  * Kubernetes (kubernetes)
  * Apple (apple)
  * MicroSandbox (microsandbox)
  * Lima (lima)
  * OrbStack (orbstack)
  * SSH (ssh)
  * AWS (aws)
  * Google Cloud (gcloud)
  * Azure (azure)
  * Digital Ocean (digitalocean)

List what is available from the CLI:

Copy Text

    `devsy provider list --available`

## Add a providerCopy Anchor Link

### Devsy DesktopCopy Anchor Link

Open Providers and click Add. The wizard has four steps:

  1. Select. Pick a preset, or enter a GitHub link, a `provider.yaml` URL, or a local path under Provider Source.
  2. Configure. Fill in the options. The form comes from the provider's schema.
  3. Initialize. Devsy runs the provider init and streams the logs.
  4. Done. Review the result. A failure shows the underlying error.

Click a provider in the list to edit its settings, switch version, update, re-initialize, rename, set it as default, or delete it.

### Devsy CLICopy Anchor Link

Copy Text

    `devsy provider add docker`

Use `--name` to add the same provider more than once with different options:

Copy Text

    `devsy provider add aws --name aws-gpu -o AWS_INSTANCE_TYPE=p3.8xlarge`

From GitHub. Devsy downloads the `provider.yaml` from the latest release. It uses your local HTTPS credentials, so private repositories work. Add `@` and a tag for another release.

Copy Text

    `devsy provider add devsy-org/devsy-provider-terraform
    devsy provider add my-org/[email protected]`

From a local path or URL.

Copy Text

    `devsy provider add ../devsy-provider-mock/provider.yaml
    devsy provider add https://github.com/devsy-org/devsy-provider-ssh/releases/download/v0.0.3/provider.yaml`

To keep using the built-in one, add it explicitly:

Copy Text

    `devsy provider add builtin:microsandbox --name legacy-microsandbox --use=false`

If a switch fails during initialization, the new source stays selected. Fix the cause and run `devsy provider init <name>`, or set the previous source again. Add `--version <tag>` to `set-source` to pin a release.

## Set provider optionsCopy Anchor Link

Each provider has its own options. In the desktop app, open Providers and click Edit on a provider. With the CLI, set options when you add or initialize:

Copy Text

    `devsy provider add <provider-nam e> -o KEY=value
    devsy provider init <provider-nam e> -o KEY=value`

List the options and their current values:

Copy Text

    `devsy provider get <provider-nam e>`

Change one later:

Copy Text

    `devsy provider set <provider-nam e> --option KEY=VALUE`

## Docker providerCopy Anchor Link

Devsy follows the Docker CLI's rules for contexts and daemon endpoints. It keeps your existing Docker `config.json` and contexts, so contexts from Docker Desktop, OrbStack, or a remote endpoint keep working.

Devsy picks the connection in the same order as the Docker CLI:

  1. `DOCKER_CONTEXT`
  2. `DOCKER_HOST`
  3. The active context in `$DOCKER_CONFIG/config.json`, or `~/.docker/config.json` when `DOCKER_CONFIG` is not set
  4. The local socket, `unix:///var/run/docker.sock`

Set `DOCKER_CONTEXT` or `DOCKER_HOST` as a provider option or as an environment variable:

Copy Text

    `devsy provider set docker -o DOCKER_CONTEXT=<context-nam e>
    devsy provider set docker -o DOCKER_HOST=ssh://user@docker-host`

For a remote TCP daemon with mutual TLS, set `DOCKER_TLS_VERIFY=1` and point `DOCKER_CERT_PATH` at your client certificates.

### Rancher DesktopCopy Anchor Link

Rancher Desktop works with the Docker provider when it uses the Moby engine. If you use `containerd`, switch to Moby. On macOS Devsy looks for the CLI at `~/.rd/bin/docker` when `docker` is not on your `PATH`. You can set both values yourself:

Copy Text

    `devsy provider set docker -o DOCKER_PATH="$HOME/.rd/bin/docker"
    devsy provider set docker -o REDACTED`

## Single machineCopy Anchor Link

By default each workspace gets its own machine. To share one machine between all workspaces on a provider, turn on Reuse machine in the provider's options in the desktop app, or run:

Copy Text

    `devsy provider init <provider-nam e> --single-machine`

## Default providerCopy Anchor Link

Devsy uses the default provider for workspaces that do not name one. Set it in the provider's options in the desktop app, or run:

Copy Text

    `devsy provider use <provider-nam e>`

## Update a providerCopy Anchor Link

Show available versions. Add `--prerelease` to include pre-releases and `--no-cache` to skip the version cache.

Copy Text

    `devsy provider versions <nam e>`

Fetch the provider's source again. Registry entries and unpinned GitHub repositories resolve to the latest release; a pinned tag fetches that version. Local paths and direct `provider.yaml` URLs reload that source.

Copy Text

    `devsy provider set-source <nam e>`

Pin a version, or replace the source:

Copy Text

    `devsy provider set-source <nam e> --version v0.2.0
    devsy provider set-source <nam e> my-org/my-repo
    devsy provider set-source <nam e> https://path/to/provider.yaml
    devsy provider set-source <nam e> ../path-to/provider.yaml`

In the desktop app, use the provider's Select version, Update, and Initialize actions.

Existing workspaces keep the provider version they were created with. Recreate one with `devsy workspace up <name> --recreate` to pick up the new version.

## Remove a providerCopy Anchor Link

In the desktop app, click the trash icon on the provider. If a workspace uses it, Devsy asks you to remove that workspace first. With the CLI:

Copy Text

    `devsy provider delete <provider-nam e>`

Delete or move the provider's workspaces first. Otherwise you cannot use them until you add the provider again.

## Rename a providerCopy Anchor Link

Copy Text

    `devsy provider rename <current-nam e> <new-nam e>`

Workspaces, machines, options, and the default setting follow the new name. If any step fails, Devsy rolls the rename back.

  * The new name must be unique and can use lowercase letters, numbers, and dashes, up to 32 characters.
  * Pro providers cannot be renamed.
  * Stop the provider's workspaces first.

In the desktop app, edit Provider Name in the provider's configuration and click Update Options.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
